727
01:14:50.653 --> 01:14:52.827
Oh, fuck, Flamingo!

728
01:14:53.060 --> 01:14:56.827
He seemed like a good kid, you know,
and you said you were just going to talk.

729
01:14:57.627 --> 01:15:00.063
- He was calling the cops.
- Jesus Christ.

730
01:15:00.163 --> 01:15:02.365
- Well, what about the intel?
- Ginette's, 9:00 a.m.

731
01:15:02.465 --> 01:15:05.768
Okay. Well, he's clearly dead, Flamingo.

732
01:15:05.868 --> 01:15:08.565
The last thing I want to be doing tonight
is digging this poor kid a shallow grave.

733
01:15:08.665 --> 01:15:11.193
- So put him in the tub.
- Good idea.

734
01:15:16.396 --> 01:15:18.882
It's the end of the road, Gwenny.

735
01:15:18.982 --> 01:15:23.653
One of us has to answer for all that's
gone down since you went sideways.

736
01:15:23.753 --> 01:15:26.956
But I ain't going to jail
for shit I never done.

737
01:15:27.056 --> 01:15:28.891
Oh, you done plenty, Cyrus.

738
01:15:28.991 --> 01:15:32.626
Think about it. What really
happened at your place?

739
01:15:40.303 --> 01:15:45.439
Aster! Aster, we have to go!
They're gonna kill us!

740
01:15:48.601 --> 01:15:49.889
Aster!

741
01:15:50.480 --> 01:15:55.815
Unfortunately, my survival
instincts outweigh my loyalty.

742
01:15:56.686 --> 01:16:00.457
And the world only believes
the last man standing.

743
01:16:00.657 --> 01:16:05.913
Don't worry, though,
you'll look great in the papers.

744
01:16:06.013 --> 01:16:07.260
<i>Aster!</i>

745
01:16:24.847 --> 01:16:27.380
Just tell me you did it.

746
01:16:28.117 --> 01:16:31.821
Tell me you killed Aster. Just say it.

747
01:16:32.221 --> 01:16:34.854
Probably didn't even pull the trigger.

748
01:16:36.358 --> 01:16:38.261
Just tell me who did.

749
01:16:38.961 --> 01:16:41.360
I just need to know.

750
01:16:44.133 --> 01:16:46.199
You did, honey.

751
01:17:56.472 --> 01:17:58.141
Would you have said yes?

752
01:17:58.741 --> 01:18:00.593
Yes.

753
01:18:00.893 --> 01:18:04.357
Yes. I say yes, I say yes, I say yes.

754
01:18:05.181 --> 01:18:07.168
<i>I say yes!</i>

755
01:18:48.590 --> 01:18:50.890
Gwen! Gwenny.

756
01:19:30.741 --> 01:19:32.798
It was you.

757
01:19:33.269 --> 01:19:35.474
But you can tell them...

758
01:19:35.982 --> 01:19:38.014
it was me.

759
01:21:16.406 --> 01:21:20.877
I don't know. I was always thinking
that I'd go to Mexico or something,

760
01:21:20.977 --> 01:21:25.048
you know, and start, like,
selling scooters, or something like that.

761
01:21:25.148 --> 01:21:28.329
Or, oh, I could totally become
a professional poker player,

762
01:21:28.429 --> 01:21:30.821
- those guys make crazy money.
- Do you play poker?

763
01:21:30.921 --> 01:21:32.655
That's not the point, Flamingo!

764
01:21:32.755 --> 01:21:35.091
The point is, it's all about luck,
and I have a horseshoe up my ass.

765
01:21:35.191 --> 01:21:37.292
I'm going to sail across the ocean.

766
01:21:37.392 --> 01:21:39.542
- That's random.
- Are you ready?

767
01:21:39.661 --> 01:21:41.682
Oh. Of course I'm ready, Flamingo.

768
01:21:41.782 --> 01:21:44.300
The intel we got from your boy, Winks,
I mean, that's airtight,

769
01:21:44.400 --> 01:21:46.405
and I'm sure as shit not going
to let that poor kid die in vain.

770
01:21:46.505 --> 01:21:48.805
- The plan?
- Okay, the plan.

771
01:21:48.905 --> 01:21:52.075
You hole up in the diner, I station
myself in the El Camino around back,

772
01:21:52.175 --> 01:21:55.378
when Cyrus shows up, I'm gonna
honk twice, that's your cue.

773
01:21:55.478 --> 01:21:58.071
You wait 10 seconds, you get up,
you walk through the kitchen,

774
01:21:58.171 --> 01:22:00.355
you execute the son of a bitch.
You keep on walking,

775
01:22:00.455 --> 01:22:02.707
you hop in the El Camino with me,
we drive off into the sunset.

776
01:22:02.807 --> 01:22:05.755
- And Bob's your uncle.
- Don't fuck up.

777
01:22:05.855 --> 01:22:07.965
- You got a way with words, girly.
- Ty?

778
01:22:08.065 --> 01:22:10.676
- Yeah?
- Nothing.

779
01:22:13.029 --> 01:22:15.264
Sail across the ocean?
Don't sound too shabby.

780
01:22:15.364 --> 01:22:17.800
Maybe... I'll join my lady friend.

781
01:22:17.900 --> 01:22:20.135
- Who might that be?
- You.

782
01:22:20.372 --> 01:22:22.402
Two honks.

783
01:22:24.539 --> 01:22:25.905
Two honks!

784
01:22:41.123 --> 01:22:44.356
Bless your soul.
Beautiful day, ain't it?

785
01:22:49.665 --> 01:22:51.697
Sure is, old man.

786
01:22:56.189 --> 01:22:57.406
Coffee, sweetie?

787
01:22:57.506 --> 01:23:01.641
Milk, early bird number two, pancakes.

788
01:23:07.016 --> 01:23:09.285
Hiya, fellas. Y'all gonna
be having the usual, today?

789
01:23:09.585 --> 01:23:12.986
- You betcha, Mary.
- So, three usuals coming right up.

790
01:23:28.103 --> 01:23:30.940
<i>All right, and we're back. Next up,
we have one of my favorite oldies.</i>

791
01:23:31.040 --> 01:23:35.078
<i>Always takes me back to the very
first time I heard it. Enjoy.</i>
